{
  "_readme": [
    "Named location archetypes: the distinct ways a pitch type actually gets used.",
    "Replaces picking a random zone edge, which made every slider trace the same arc.",
    "",
    "Keyed by pitch type, then platoon matchup:",
    "  same = pitcher and batter same-handed (RHP vs RHB, LHP vs LHB)",
    "  opp  = opposite-handed (RHP vs LHB, LHP vs RHB)",
    "Platoon rather than batter hand because LHP-vs-LHB mirrors RHP-vs-RHB, and",
    "because a pitch's break direction relative to the batter is what changes.",
    "",
    "Coordinates are batter-relative, in units of zone half-width / half-height",
    "measured from the zone center:",
    "  in_away  +1.0 = inside edge (toward the batter), -1.0 = outside edge",
    "  height   +1.0 = top of zone, -1.0 = bottom of zone",
    "Pitcher.in_sign() flips in_away into screen pixels, so the same archetype",
    "works for both batter hands without duplicated data.",
    "",
    "intent must be one of zone/edge/chase/waste and ties the archetype to the",
    "calibrated INTENT_TABLE mix in pitcher.py -- archetypes choose WHERE within",
    "an intent, they do not change how often each intent is used. Keep an",
    "archetype for every intent a pitch uses, or it falls back to generic",
    "geometry. 'counts' multiplies the weight in the named count states."
  ],

